// The Autonomous Enterprise — Lists panel (v1.0 shipped all six originally-planned phases;
// v1.2.2 below adds a fourth top-level entry as part of the separately-approved v1.2
// feature set — see NOTES.md)
//
// One plugin binding (unchanged since v0.2): the ai-text-plugin, aliased `generateText`,
// matching examples/office-clicker/lists.txt:3 (`generateText = {import:ai-text-plugin}`).
// It has THREE independent consumers in html.txt: the read-only v0.2 "Slack" feed, the
// v0.6 crisis engine (parses a strict-format response, DOES mutate game state), and the
// v0.8 morning briefing (prompted with an exact delta string, narrates it, never mutates
// state itself). v1.0 adds a FOURTH major mechanic — prestige/meta-progression — that
// uses NONE of this: no new plugin, no new AI call, no new Lists-panel content at all.
// It's pure client-side JS reading/writing a second localStorage key. See NOTES.md.
//
// Three flat data lists: devTraits/marketerTraits (added in v0.4), plus employeeNames
// (added in v1.2.2). Same shape as apps/discovery-question-generator/lists.txt's
// `persona`/`vertical` lists: bare items, 2-space-indented, the label doubles as the value
// (`examples/pixelsaga/lists.txt:19-40`). html.txt reads a random trait or name via
// `root[listName].selectOne.evaluateItem` at first-feature time — the exact `dqgPick()`
// idiom from `apps/discovery-question-generator/html.txt:149-151`, cited there to
// `examples/pixelsaga/html.txt:2562-2571` — feeding the feed and crisis prompts. Not used
// by the v0.8 briefing or the v1.0 prestige layer, both deliberately independent of it.
//
// Everything else — state, tick math, UI, save/load, feed, crisis, offline delta
// capture/briefing, and now the Boardroom/IPO/patent logic — lives in html.txt. This is
// the sixth and final planned phase; see NOTES.md for the complete build history.

generateText = {import:ai-text-plugin} // "Slack" feed (read-only), crisis text (mutates via a parsed choice), morning briefing (narrates deltas already applied) — see NOTES.md

// Assigned randomly to a developer at hire time (aentHireDeveloper in html.txt) and
// stored on that worker for the rest of the session/save. Terms lean into the
// "Office Politics" framing the user's own v0.4 spec used as its example.
devTraits
  Pragmatic
  Perfectionist
  Chaotic
  Overcaffeinated
  Meticulous

// Assigned randomly to a marketer at hire time (aentHireMarketer in html.txt).
marketerTraits
  Aggressive
  Diplomatic
  Data-Driven
  Charismatic
  Burned-Out

// v1.2.2: flat bare-item name pool, same shape as devTraits/marketerTraits above (not a
// new DSL idiom). Resolved lazily onto a worker the first time they're featured in a
// feed/crisis narrative — aentResolveName in html.txt, mirroring aentResolveTrait exactly.
// Generic first names only, no NSTSP branding, no real people. Duplicate names across
// different workers are accepted by design; see NOTES.md v1.2.2.
employeeNames
  Dana
  Sam
  Jordan
  Casey
  Riley
  Morgan
  Alex
  Taylor
  Jamie
  Avery
  Quinn
  Reese
  Skyler
  Drew
  Emerson

